// @consolidated-test (generated by consolidate_tests.py)
/*
 * coverage_extra_test.cj — interface-coverage top-up for eudi_cjmdoc_security.
 *
 * Targets public symbols not yet exercised by the existing *_test.cj suites,
 * with real offline assertions (no aa-test / device dependency unless noted):
 *
 *   SessionEncryption.forMdoc            — factory wiring (peer key + private key)
 *   SessionEncryption.sessionTranscript  — instance ST built from the wired raw bytes
 *   SessionEncryption.sessionTranscriptBytes — Tag24(ST) used as HKDF salt
 *   CoseMac0.toCborArray                 — 4-element CBOR value shape (not just bytes)
 *   DigestCalculations.validateDigestsForNamespace — success + missing + failed branches
 *   MsoValidation.validateDocType        — match / mismatch
 *   SoftwareSecureArea.getStorage        — storage round-trip identity
 *   SoftwareSecureArea.unlockKey         — software keys need no unlock (None)
 *   SoftwareSecureArea.defaultSigningAlgorithm — curve → algorithm mapping
 *   mdocSecurityModuleAnchor             — module-anchor smoke (returns Unit, no throw)
 *
 * makeEckaDHAgreement is intentionally NOT exercised here: it routes through
 * EcdhP256.agree() → HUKS, which is device-only (no host/offline KAT possible).
 * Its HKDF consumer path is already covered via synthetic shared secrets in the
 * session / device-auth suites.
 *
 * cjc 1.1.3 notes honored: Array<T>(n, repeat: x); no-space byte literals like
 * [0xA0u8]; bare-array typed lets; .isNone()/.isSome(); @Expect(a,b); match.
 */
